@tradition rec-dawn-swim
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Dawn swim: Tuesdays and Thursdays 06:15-06:45 from Day 2, the pool; Rina, before the infirmary opens. Tap a lane.
// FOR RA: the pool's lane type is yours (written here as rec:lane; four lanes, then the loungers / pool edge as waiting
// spots). Intended who: swimmer (RA's habit) 80%.
k: 488
title: Dawn swim
when: weekly tuesday,thursday from day 2
at: 06:15-06:45
min: 20
wake: 15
where: 7 room Pool: rec:lane
who: rina always, infirmary 25%, juniors 15%, everyone 5%
anim: everyone water
host: rina
from: rina
flag: rec.on

== mail
- Dawn swim tomorrow, {time} at the pool. Empty lanes, quiet water, done before the infirmary opens. Rina will be there. She always is.

== ask
- Dawn swim in the morning. Quarter past six. Don't think about it. Just come.
- Swim before breakfast? You feel brilliant all day. Annoyingly brilliant.   #funny

== here
- Lanes are lovely at this hour.
- Four lengths, then breakfast. That's the deal.
- Nobody talks. It's the best bit.   #warm

== thanks
- You slip into an empty lane while the ship's still waking. The water's warm and the stars are right there.   #warm

== chatter
- Dawn swim's the best start to a day. Ask Rina. Actually don't, she'll make you come.   #funny
- I went to dawn swim once. Once. My alarm still hasn't forgiven me.   #funny
- Rina swims faster than she walks.
